class:: HarmonicVariation
summary:: Change in the harmonic amplitude distribution
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/HarmonicDeviation, Classes/FFTFlux2, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Shared interpolated spectral peaks are associated with the nearest integer harmonic of the supplied F0. Only the strongest matching peak occupies each harmonic slot. Missing harmonics retain zero slots; an incorrect F0 or tight tolerance changes the result. The formulas are explicit MIRa conventions in the harmonic-descriptor tradition summarized by Peeters (2004); this is independent code, not a wrapper around another analysis library. Measures one minus cosine similarity between current and previous harmonic-slot amplitude vectors. Common gain changes leave it at zero. The first usable frame and frames after missing harmonic evidence return zero. Frequency changes that preserve the harmonic amplitude pattern do not count as variation.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain. This analyzer updates when a new frame arrives and holds its output between frames.

argument:: f0
Supplied fundamental in Hz, for example the first output of Pitch2. Nonpositive or invalid values disable harmonic association.

argument:: maxHarmonics
Literal number of harmonic slots from 1 through 64. Harmonic index is stable when partials are missing.

argument:: tolerance
Maximum distance in cents between a peak and its nearest integer multiple of f0, clamped from 0 through 600. Default 50.

argument:: peakThreshold
Minimum local-peak magnitude relative to the largest included spectral peak, from 0 through 1. Up to 128 strongest peaks are retained.

argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two from 256 through 8192, matching the FFT buffer. Frequency resolution and first-result latency depend on this size.

returns::
Variation from 0 through 1.

method:: fromAudio
Convenience constructor: accepts audio and builds Pitch2 plus FFT internally, then calls kr with the estimated F0. The input range defaults to 55 through 1760 Hz, FFT size 4096 and hop fraction 0.25; it accepts the same harmonic controls. Use kr when sharing an existing pitch estimate or FFT chain.

examples::
HarmonicVariation measures the frame-to-frame normalized spectral correlation distance across harmonic partials, quantifying timbral flux independent of pitch or loudness. In this example, it triggers a granular micro-delay particle generator whenever the harmonic timbre shifts: steady sustains remain clean, while expressive articulation and vibrato generate fluttering grain clouds. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: plots the variation index.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1600, 2048, 0.25);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var variation = HarmonicVariation.kr(chain, pitch[0], maxHarmonics: 16, fftSize: 2048);
        var varSmooth = variation.lag(0.03);

        // Granular bursts triggered by rapid harmonic variation
        var grainBurst = Dust2.ar(varSmooth * 400);
        var granules = Ringz.ar(grainBurst, pitch[0].clip(100, 2000) * [1.5, 2.0], 0.03).sum * 0.15;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + granules;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, variation) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Harmonic Variation", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
